    "text": "STORAGE LOSES PART OF THE CROP: the ICAR onion and garlic institute says 30 to 40% of stored onion gets lost; up to 42% over four months in a thatched store and up to 46% in a ventilated one (about 55 to 59% in its 120-day trial of ventilated and bulk storage); 5% in a cold store at 0 °C, though 27% of those onions sprouted within 15 days of coming out; and 7.14% in the institute's own store kept at about 27 °C. These are the institute's statements and trials, not losses measured on farms in Nashik."
